{
  "slug": "marcopolo",
  "name": "Marcopolo",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "MarcoPolo is a data computer that connects to your databases, warehouses, cloud storage, and SaaS applications, and provides a workspace where AI can query, correlate, analyze, and act on that data. The MarcoPolo plugin is the most effective way to connect Claude to this computer - it bundles the MCP connection with skills and a subagent that guide Claude through proven data workflows.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 skills**, **1 agent** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (4): `query-and-analyze` (Queries connections, joins results across sources through DuckDB, and analyzes workspace data), `setup-connection` (Adds a new connection to the MarcoPolo workspace — hosted demo connections (no credentials) and credentialed connections to…), `using-connection-cli` (Reference for the in-workspace `connection` CLI — verb shape, JSON envelope, the capability rule, and per-verb flag details), `using-marcopolo-workspace` (Orientation for the MarcoPolo remote workspace, what it is, how `/workspace` is laid out, when to use the…)\n- **Agents** (1): `marcopolo` (Data analyst that works with company data in a remote MarcoPolo workspace)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `MarcoPolo`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install marcopolo@claude-community` from `immersa-co/marcopolo-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 4,
    "agent": 1,
    "mcp": 1
  },
